1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,411
A parent asks:

2
00:00:01,411 --> 00:00:05,408
my kid is sitting an extra university interview on top of the gaokao.

3
00:00:05,408 --> 00:00:07,320
Does it actually change anything?

4
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:08,941
Let's open the file.

5
00:00:09,261 --> 00:00:13,247
Exhibit A: XJTLU's 2026 brochure for Jiangsu.

6
00:00:13,247 --> 00:00:16,258
The composite score is out of 100.

7
00:00:16,578 --> 00:00:20,225
The gaokao, scaled to 100, counts for 65 percent.

8
00:00:20,225 --> 00:00:23,575
The university's own interview counts for 35.

9
00:00:23,895 --> 00:00:27,537
Now a hypothetical reconstruction. Student A:

10
00:00:27,537 --> 00:00:32,556
600 on the gaokao, 90 in the interview. Student B: 615 and 70.

11
00:00:32,876 --> 00:00:39,788
Scaled from 750, A comes to 83.50. B comes to 77.80.

12
00:00:40,108 --> 00:00:43,479
B led by fifteen gaokao points, and still finishes behind.

13
00:00:44,599 --> 00:00:47,564
Finding one: the interview is points you can prepare for.

14
00:00:47,884 --> 00:00:48,600
Two caveats.

15
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,703
This example predicts nothing about real admissions.

16
00:00:52,023 --> 00:00:55,906
And your gaokao score must first clear the special-category control line.

17
00:00:56,226 --> 00:00:59,928
Exhibits B and C. XJTLU: if you're not admitted this way,

18
00:00:59,928 --> 00:01:03,501
you can still apply in the regular undergraduate round.

19
00:01:03,821 --> 00:01:06,786
CUHK-Shenzhen: it doesn't affect your later applications.

20
00:01:07,106 --> 00:01:09,581
Finding two: one more chance to be admitted.

21
00:01:09,901 --> 00:01:11,202
But check the jurisdiction.

22
00:01:11,522 --> 00:01:15,512
In Guangdong, the same university uses 65 for the gaokao,

23
00:01:15,512 --> 00:01:18,523
30 for the interview, 5 for academic tests,

24
00:01:18,523 --> 00:01:20,973
and the deadline moves to May 20th.

25
00:01:21,293 --> 00:01:23,384
Always check the province and the year.

26
00:01:23,704 --> 00:01:26,738
It also costs time: applications in April and May,

27
00:01:26,738 --> 00:01:29,165
and the interview soon after the gaokao.

28
00:01:29,485 --> 00:01:32,479
Exhibit D, on the interview: it assesses English,

29
00:01:32,479 --> 00:01:35,778
overall competence and ability, not subject knowledge.

30
00:01:36,098 --> 00:01:38,472
So the skill to practise is simple: a view,

31
00:01:38,472 --> 00:01:39,853
and the reason behind it.

32
00:01:40,173 --> 00:01:41,418
Write only an opinion,

33
00:01:41,418 --> 00:01:44,531
and the feedback flags the missing reason. Add because,

34
00:01:44,531 --> 00:01:45,720
and that flag clears.

35
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:51,161
Verdict: one more assessment, and one more chance,

36
00:01:51,161 --> 00:01:53,773
paid for with a threshold, time and preparation.

37
00:01:54,093 --> 00:01:56,938
Before you apply, check three things: your province,

38
00:01:56,938 --> 00:02:00,002
the control line, and your time to prepare. Case closed.
